# Advanced Data Analysis, KPI Development & Business Intelligence Dashboard
### AnalystLab Africa — Data Analytics Internship | Week 3

An advanced, multi-KPI Power BI dashboard continuing the [Global Superstore dataset](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/apoorvaappz/global-super-store-dataset) analysis from Week 2, going deeper into profitability, discounting behaviour, and regional/product-level performance for a global retail client.

## Business Problem

Following the executive overview delivered in Week 2, leadership requested a deeper analysis to identify what is actually driving — and limiting — profitability across markets, categories, and products, and to translate those findings into concrete, evidence-based recommendations.

## Approach

1. **Project Continuity** — reviewed Week 2 findings and identified specific areas requiring deeper investigation
2. **Advanced Business Analysis** — discount impact, product-level performance, time-based trends, regional depth, and customer segment profitability
3. **KPI & DAX Development** — 6 KPIs and 9 DAX measures, including profit margin, average discount, and loss-making order/product counts
4. **Time-Based Analysis** — monthly, quarterly, and yearly sales and profit trends
5. **Business Problem Investigation** — 4 specific problems identified and investigated with supporting evidence
6. **Interactive Dashboard** — a single-page Power BI dashboard with 12+ visualisations and 5 slicers
7. **Business Insights & Recommendations** — 6 insights and 6 evidence-based recommendations

## Key Findings

| Driver | Finding |
|---|---|
| Discounting | Average profit per order turns **negative beyond a 20% discount**, with losses deepening sharply past 40% |
| Product performance | **65 products** generate over $10,000 in sales each while still posting a net loss |
| Regional | **EMEA** has the lowest profit margin of any market (5.4%) and the highest average discount (20%) — the two are directly linked |
| Segment | **Home Office** is the most efficient segment by margin (12.0%), even though Consumer leads on total volume |
| Seasonality | **Q4** (Sep–Dec) is the strongest quarter in every year of the dataset without exception |

## Tools

- **Microsoft Power BI** (Power Query, DAX, data modelling, interactive dashboards, scatter/matrix/treemap visuals)
